// Parse a single CSV record (one logical row) from a stream of characters.
// - Fields are separated by the given delimiter (default ',').
// - Fields may be enclosed in double quotes.
// - Inside a quoted field, a literal quote is represented by two consecutive quotes ("").
// - Newlines inside a quoted field are part of the field value.
// - Leading/trailing whitespace outside quotes is NOT trimmed.
//
// The function receives the FULL text (which may contain multiple rows)
// and a reference to a position index.  It parses ONE logical row starting
// at pos, advances pos past the row (including the terminating newline if any),
// and returns the fields of that row.
//
// If pos >= text.size(), returns an empty vector (no more rows).
std::vector<std::string> parse_csv_row(const std::string& text, size_t& pos, char delim = ',') {

golden_completion:
